<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dax</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Aquae Tarbellicae</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dax is a spa town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adour">Adour</a> in the Landes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. As <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aquae-tarbellicae">Aquae Tarbellicae</a> it was the chief town of the Aquitanian Tarbelli and became famous under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> for its hot springs, still used for thermal cures. Parts of its late Roman walls survive, and it was the seat of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> from late antiquity.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dax.jpg" alt="Dax" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AubdaX · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dax,_Fontaine_Chaude.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
